GUL is the only released variant (A21 §1 / A22 §3: "SUL-GUL (GUL only; SUL not released)", released code defaults,
500 epochs). The port evalpaper/ext/SUL-GUL/run_method.py (UncertaintyGLAD src @1a1f2e4, unmodified + the
matplotlib stub) is imported READ-ONLY: load_gul and resolve_hparams are reused (README MUTAG demo = argparse defaults,
poll_ratio recorded as 0 = normal-only mode, realised by the normal-only typed training data). The training loop (the
port's line-by-line copy of src/main.py:run_split()) is copied here with # CHANGE-TYPED marks:
  * data = typed_data; UB-GOLD set_seed(3407 + seed) before the model; topk = min(96, n_fit) = 96 here (n_fit >= 400,
    so the A19 topk fallback never applies);
  * GUL evaluates after every epoch: each group's test set (test normals + T) is one unshuffled loader of
